--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
could not be evaluated
expected constant expression
--
The constant evaluator gave up on a call of a constructor or member
function on a local object (`S s("abcd"); s.cut_twice();'): such calls
are now evaluated with `this' bound to the local's tracked value, which
the call updates.  Compound assignments and increments of a member
(`n -= k', `++n') are applied too.  This made libstdc++ 16.2.0's
<format> lose __do_vformat_to<_Sink_iter<wchar_t>, ...>.
